Subject: [PATCH] cli: POST /api/v1/renew renews radios named by agent AL MAC and current class

em_cli had no way to renew a radio: its server has no renew route, and the CLI's cfg_renew
reached the controller as a radio MAC read from the subdoc's name (series 0258). A renew is
how a lab proves what an agent does with a fresh M2 for one radio, without renewing every
radio of the network as a network SSID change does.

The route takes {"devices": [{"al_mac": ..., "classes": [...]}]}, checks it
(renew_request.go), and sends the controller the wfa-dataelements:Renew subdoc through
libemcli's cfg_renew with the caller's tree (submitRenewSubdoc). The controller checks the
request as a whole; the route answers 202 with the radios requested, 400 for a request that
is not well formed, 422 when the controller refuses it, 503 when it is not ready.

Upstream-Status: Pending

diff --git a/src/rdkb-cli/main.go b/src/rdkb-cli/main.go
